Date: Thu, 25 Feb 93 10:44:45 CST
From: eder@hsvaic.boeing.com (Dani Eder)
Subject: EXT: Selective breeding

As I have pointed out before, if there are any subpopulations 
carrying memes for high birth-rate, then they will eventually
dominate the population.  The best example in the US is the
Latter Day Saints (Mormons).  They number several million,
mostly in the western states around Utah.  

While the US as a whole has 21% of the population under 15
years of age, Alaska has 28, Idaho 26, Wyoming 26, and Utah 32.
The U.S. population growth rate is 0.7% per year, while the
rate for Utah is 1.8%, abut the average for the world as a whole.
The high population growth rate in Utah can be mostly attributed
to the large number of children born there.

If this growth rate differential persisted for a century, then
the couple of million Mormons would grow to six times as many.
Of course, we extropians expect events to render such questions
moot before then, don't we?

Dani Eder

