_The Selfish Gene_ does not argue this; in fact quite the opposite: 
genetic fitness is measured by the number of genes propagated to
the next generation.  It is unlikely that in any developed
country well-educated women benefit their sibs' fertility to
any significant extent.  The effect would have to be quite dramatic 
to counterbalance their lack of genetic fitness vs. high school dropouts, 
which is almost a 1:2 ratio.   Their sibs would have to have 4 times
as many children as the sibs of high school dropouts for their genetic
fitness to catch up!

